@title Lease or Buy the Digital Press
@subtitle Orchard Press. Decision for Lucinda Marsh, owner, at the meeting on 2026-11-12

# Options

The press prints about 2.4 million pages a month. We compare two ways to get a digital press over a four-year horizon.

- **Buy:** purchase for $412,000, plus a service contract at $14,400 a year.
- **Lease:** $7,650 a month for 48 months, with service included. A deposit of two monthly payments ($15,300) applies, and an optional buyout at the end costs $95,000.

# Four-year cost

table = Item,Buy,Lease; Up-front cash,"$412,000 purchase price","$15,300 deposit"; Service,"$57,600 over four years",Included; Resale or buyout,"$120,000 expected resale (a guess)","$95,000 optional buyout (fixed today)"; Four-year total,"$349,600 net of resale","$367,200"

Buying comes to $349,600 over four years after resale. Leasing comes to $367,200. The lease costs $17,600 more over four years.

# Risks

- Buying ties up cash we need for the new bindery, and the resale value is a guess.
- The lease locks us in for 48 months, although the buyout price is fixed today.

# Recommendation

We recommend the lease. It costs $17,600 more over four years than buying, and we say so plainly. In return it needs no large cash outlay, so cash stays free for the new bindery.
